@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+---
+id: dl-004-applymergepatch-semantics-pure-strict-json-input-own-members-only
+type: decision-log
+title: "applyMergePatch semantics: pure, strict JSON input, own members only"
+status: pending
+---
+
+## Context
+
+RFC 7386 defines MergePatch(Target, Patch) but leaves open aliasing of inputs, invalid input, and
+special member names.
+
+## Decision
+
+- Pure: neither argument is mutated and the result shares no structure with them (values are cloned).
+- Target and patch must be JSON values (same check as `applyPatch`); otherwise it throws.
+- Only own members of the target are considered, and members are set with `defineProperty`, so
+  `__proto__` and names such as `toString` are ordinary keys.
+- Following the RFC, a non-object target meets an object patch as `{}`, so `null` members inside a
+  patch applied there are dropped; arrays are replaced wholesale.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Callers get a safe merge at the cost of a copy per call. A `null` value cannot be set through a merge
+patch, as the RFC specifies.
